# UC-005 · Cache

> Partial of `docs/use-cases/UC-005-get-account-balance/`. Owner: `cache-architect`.
> Inherits the freshness tolerance from `00-caso-de-uso.md` and the ports from `10-dominio.md` —
> doesn't redecide them. Contains no code. Form references in
> `.claude/skills/cache-architect/templates/`.
> Rules applied, never reproduced: `@.claude/rules/caching.md`.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Mother spec | `00-caso-de-uso.md` |
| Why this partial exists | `00-caso-de-uso.md` § Freshness: "a balance may be up to 30 seconds old" |
| Cache package | `adapter.out.cache` (blueprint `packages.map`) |
| Divergences from other partials | none |

## 1 · Cached reads

| Read (port method) | Cache name | Key — every input that changes the result | Value | Freshness tolerance | Absence cached | Concurrent misses |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `AccountRepositoryPort.findBalance(ownerId, accountId)` | `account-balance` | `ownerId + ':' + accountId` — the owner is a parameter: the use case passes the authenticated owner it already checked | `AccountBalanceView` (record, plain components, declared next to the port) | 30 s | no — `unless = "#result == null"` | computed per caller — `sync` is refused next to `unless`, and one balance is not hot enough to need it |

Authorization sits above this port, in the use case: a hit never skips it.

## 2 · Provider

| Decision | Value | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Provider | Redis | Replicas = 2 (inherited from `20-persistencia.md` § 1 `Claim strategy`). A local cache would evict on the writing instance only, and the other one would serve the old balance for a whole expiry — inside 30 s, but `references/provider-decision-matrix.md` § 2 row 2 picks the shared copy whenever an eviction must reach every instance |
| Transaction-aware | yes | The write (`save`) runs inside the deposit and withdrawal use cases' transactions; the eviction waits for the commit |
| Inherited? | no — first cache of this project | `pom.xml` carries no cache dependency; no earlier `22-cache.md` |

Rejected, one line each: **Caffeine** — two replicas and an eviction that must reach both.
**Two-level (Caffeine over Redis)** — no read hot enough to justify a second copy and its
invalidation broadcast. **Hibernate second-level cache** — the balance is a query-shaped read,
not an entity by id.

## 3 · Expiry and size

| Cache | Expiry | Tolerance it serves | Maximum size | Jitter | Refresh ahead |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `account-balance` | `PT30S` | 30 s | — (distributed) | up to a tenth, subtracted | no |

## 4 · Invalidation

Every writer of the data each cache holds — not only this case's.

| Writer | Writes | Path | Eviction | Staleness bound |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `DepositMoneyService` (UC-003) | `Account` balance | through `AccountRepositoryPort.save` — decorated | `ownerId + ':' + accountId`, after commit | none beyond the race `caching.md` § Invalidation names, bounded by the expiry |
| `WithdrawMoneyService` (UC-004) | `Account` balance | through `AccountRepositoryPort.save` — decorated | same | same |
| `InterestAccrualJob` (UC-007, `35-jobs.md`) | every balance, nightly | **bulk `UPDATE`**, not through the port | none — accepted: the job runs at 03:00 and each entry lives 30 s, so the expiry is the bound | 30 s |

## 5 · Failure and load

| Fact | Value |
|---|---|
| Cache down | `CountingCacheErrorHandler`: logged, counted as `cache.errors`, the read goes to the database |
| Client timeout | `250ms` command, `500ms` connect — under the balance query's p99 |
| Source without the cache | The balance query is an index read on `accounts(id)`; the database holds the full read rate without the cache — measured in the load test the case's `Freshness` row cites |

## 6 · Serialization

| Cache | Serializer | Format version |
|---|---|---|
| `account-balance` | `JacksonJsonRedisSerializer<AccountBalanceView>` — typed, no default typing | `app.cache.format-version: 1` — raised when `AccountBalanceView` changes shape |

## 7 · Observability

| Metric | Alarm it exists for |
|---|---|
| `cache.gets` (tags `cache`, `result` = hit/miss) — from the binder, statistics enabled | hit ratio of `account-balance` below 50 % for 15 min: the expiry or the key is wrong |
| `cache.errors` (tag `exception`) | above zero for 5 min: Redis degraded, every read on the database |

## 8 · Declared dependencies

| Dependency | Version | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-cache` | (managed by the Boot parent) | `@EnableCaching`, the cache abstraction |
| `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-data-redis` | (managed by the Boot parent) | `RedisCacheManager`, Lettuce |

## 9 · Configuration

| Property | Value | Owner of the value |
|---|---|---|
| `spring.data.redis.host` / `port` | `${REDIS_HOST:localhost}` / `${REDIS_PORT:6379}` | this partial; the `app` container's override is `docker-architect`'s |
| `spring.data.redis.password` | `${REDIS_PASSWORD}` — no default | `@.claude/rules/secrets.md` |
| `spring.data.redis.timeout` / `connect-timeout` | `250ms` / `500ms` | this partial, § 5 |
| `app.cache.format-version` | `1` | this partial, § 6 |
| `app.cache.caches.account-balance.ttl` | `PT30S` | this partial, § 3 — bounded by `00-caso-de-uso.md` § Freshness |

Full shape in `templates/application-cache.yml.example`.

