## Design patterns

| Force or symptom | Pattern | Classes and interfaces it creates | "When not" checked |
|---|---|---|---|
| `caching.md` § Boundary — the cache wraps an outbound port the use case already depends on | Decorator | `CachedAccountRepository implements AccountRepositoryPort`, `CachedAccountRepositoryConfig` | Not a Proxy written by hand: the framework's caching proxy wraps the decorator; the decorator only exists to keep the annotations out of the persistence adapter |

One row per pattern this layer adopts, decided through
`@.claude/skills/gof-design-patterns/SKILL.md` § Design-time use. Consolidation collects this
section into `UC-NNN-spec.md`.

## Impact on approved use cases

| Approved case | Change | Why | Satisfied by |
|---|---|---|---|
| UC-007-accrue-interest | its bulk `UPDATE` leaves `account-balance` entries up to 30 s stale after 03:00 — accepted, no code change | § 4: the job bypasses the decorated port | — |

## Implementation order

1. The dependencies of § 8
2. `CacheSettings`, `CacheNames`, `CountingCacheErrorHandler`, `RedisCacheConfig` in the cache package — once per project
3. `CachedAccountRepository` and `CachedAccountRepositoryConfig` — after `AccountRepositoryPort` and its persistence adapter exist
4. Properties in `application.yml`
5. Tests — `40-testes.md`: a second read does not reach the adapter, `save` evicts after commit, two owners never share an entry
